## Actor programs

Use snippets for one-time work; actor programs own functions, shared state and React views.
{{#if (available "actor_program_create")}}
Use `actor_program_create` with the closest template; reuse its code and tests in the returned
`directory`{{#if (available "actor_program_activate")}}, then `actor_program_activate`{{/if}}{{#if (available "bash")}}. Use `bash` with `cwd: "@actors/<name>"`,
in a room `cwd: "@actors/<room>.<name>"`{{/if}}.
{{/if}}
Call functions directly; `typescript_api` gives contracts. Published functions join your tools this turn.
Bind with `self` or `@handle`; otherwise a backend creates a TypeScript actor and a pure view
uses the caller. UI functions need no model turn. Project errors arrive automatically{{#if (available "actor_program_diagnostics")}};
`actor_program_diagnostics` gives details{{/if}}. Visible views open as tabs beside Chat.
{{#if (available "actor_view_set_visibility")}}
`actor_view_set_visibility` uses the view's `ref`; hiding keeps state.
{{/if}}
{{#if (available "actor_program_controls")}}
Query `actor_program_controls` for props or `topic: "guide"` for authoring.
`topic: "state-aware"` for a `defineProgram` that waits for time, messages or files.
{{else}}
Work that waits for a time, a message or a file and then continues is a `defineProgram`.
{{/if}}
Use shadcn/ui props, `lucide-react`, Tailwind, `AppLayout`, `Stack` and responsive `Grid`.
Do not repeat app or tab titles. Put title and `Badge` in `Stack direction="row"` and related
facts in one muted `type-meta` line, not one paragraph per fact.
Use `Form` for labeled inputs (`type: "textarea"` for long answers), not custom CSS wrappers.
Adapt the `controls` SVG example (`SvgEdge`); nodes stay Tailwind app code.
